# zram-swap
### A compressed swap on /dev/zram0 for the boards whose storage the writes of a plain swap file
### would wear out. The zram module is CONFIG_ZRAM of the kernel the platform builds (a module in
### the bcm defconfigs, -m ZRAM in lfs/kernel for the generic ones): without it the unit fails at
### modprobe, visibly, instead of booting without swap in silence
PKG_VER=1.0
BUILD_PROCESS=none
PKG_TOOLCHAIN=gnu
